{"comment_id": "UgyV3ku-0XHDtfnsIHF4AaABAg", "comment_text": "The reason why your chocolate bowls turned out trash is because you have to use tempered chocolate\n\nHow to temper chocolate:\n\n1. Melt: Chop chocolate finely. Place two-thirds of the chocolate in a heatproof bowl over a double boiler (simmering water, not touching the bowl).  Heat until it reaches the maximum melting temperature for its type.\n\r\n2. Cool: Remove the bowl from heat. Add the remaining one-third of unmelted chocolate (\"seed\") in batches, stirring vigorously until fully melted and the temperature drops to the target cooling temperature. \n\r\n3. Reheat: If the chocolate is too cool or thick, briefly return the bowl to the double boiler for 5–10 seconds at a time, stirring constantly, until it reaches the working temperature. \n\r\n4. Test: Dip a knife or piece of parchment into the chocolate. If it sets within 3–5 minutes with a glossy finish, it is properly tempered\n\n(This was not written by me)", "comment_like_count": 0, "comment_published_at": "1 小時前", "snapshot_label": "t2h", "crawl_time": "2026-05-30T05:39:53Z"}
